A||||45||Fiero*101||Why do they hate our cars?||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero*101||10-29-2001||03:51 PM||||Is it just me or is where ever we go there is alwas sombody that totally hates our cars?<BR>This was a wile ago but it just came to me reading these other posts. I went to get my exhaust redone at this shop and the guy was like what is it again? and I was like its a 1986 Fiero and he was like 4 banger? and i was like No its a V6 and he said i thought only the GT came w/ a v6 and i was like no go look at my car and he was like doesnt matter much to me any way and then he looked out side the window at my car and was like how do you spell FIERO? and as i started to spell it for him(not knowing that he was being an ASS HOLE!) was like JUNK thats right Plastic JUNK!<BR>well i just looked at him and said yeah what ever can you do this for me or not and he was like i dont know maybe ill have to look up and see if i can get parts any more. Ill give you a call next week. Well as the next week came no call.<BR>So i ask you fellow Fiero lovers do you get this same treatment?<BR>and why do they think our cars are Plastic Junk??<BR>Just curious to see what you guys and girls have to say  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>sorry it was so long<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6||||reg||5
Z||000001||87FieroGTx||10-29-2001||04:05 PM|||| Simple, pure ignorance!<P> People tend to remember the bad things and not the good.<P> I was at the track the other day and a guy in a Civic in the other lane yelled WTF why do I have to race a Fiero there's no sport in than, and then half the people there started agreeing with him <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> Well 13.6 (My 2nd best ever) seconds later I was sitting at the finish line laughing my ass off waiting for him to finish <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">! When he got there he didn't even look over at me not a word from anyone for the next 3 rounds.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-29-2001||04:16 PM||||I get a mixed response.  Seems like there are a lot of "traditional motorheads" who do act like Asses when it comes to the car.  I'd guess that 99% of them have never actually driven one, or at least one that has been upkept. And it's mid-engined... they're afraid of what they don't understand.<P>On the otherhand, as of late, I have been recieving compliments from many teens who are "into" the street racing scene.  Many of the import guys are even friendly and interested.<P>I did cruise through the "ricer" hangout by myself one night and mostly just got wierd looks... only one smartass "that's a pretty fast car..." remark from some guy standing in front of his old 2-door civic hatchback.<P>Every year I attend the same "HotRod" type show with my Fiero.  What a mixed reaction that brings.  Some of the event organizers are awsome guys and come over by the car, hang out for awhile chatting.  Others, within the same group- go much out of their way to avoid even <B>looking</B> at my car... like it's a modern automotive disease.  I just take the bad with the good- my theory on my car (and I apply this to <B>all cars</B>, even ricers):  If you are passionate enough about your car to make it suit your style, your taste.  And you spend your hard-earned cash on it, then that's cool with me- even if I wouldn't do it that way myself. <P>I want to be unique... just like eveyone else.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||10-29-2001||04:18 PM||||That's awesome.  I love it when 'those' guys are put in their place.<P>I've noticed that most people either LOVE or HATE the car.  Unlike other cars, there seems to be a lot more extremes with Fieros (as opposed to people who are just indifferent).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Reality||10-29-2001||04:27 PM||||Well on the plus side, I went to a Midas the other day was going to have a new exhaust put on. But anywho, all three guys that were there came and looked at the car and said it was nice and that the Fiero was a good car to have. Two were older gents but hey I'm 21 so everyone is older!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> The other was about my age. Well just thought I would share this. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-29-2001||04:57 PM||||At the weekly 'Vette club show, there was a guy that brought his 87 SE into the show area. ***These are not really car shows, just a bunch of gearheads hanging out*** I always drive my 88, but never bring it into the show area, but I figured that if he could do it, so could I. I was very impressed with how many people had positive comments about both of our cars. His had a carbed 4.3 v6 with all the go-fast goodies and I had the new "twin tube" intake on the 3.4- several people even admitted that they had one in the back yard and wanted us to help get it running, or asked if we wanted it for parts. Many of the cars there are 40's to 50's street rods and some late model tuner cars, but most were friendly- even the 'Vette guys. The only guys that were overly critical were the ones who were just clueless as to what they were looking at.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||10-29-2001||05:04 PM||||I've run into the whole range of responses.  One guy said, "Fiero?  Has it caught fire yet?  Cuz, you know they do that."  But anyone I give a damn about likes the car.  <P>On a refreshing note, LZeitgeist and I went to a local Pontiac only car show.  LZ entered his Formula into the show, and not only did he get respect from the other Pontiac fans, he won a plaque in his class!  The organizer of the show even invited us to join their club, the Tarheel Tigers GTO Club.  His position was, it started out as a GTO club, but if it's a Pontiac, bring it on!  That's nice to see.||||reg||1
Z||000007||falconhulk||10-29-2001||05:10 PM||||heh heh heh seems like there are posts like this every week.  I have not had one person say 1 bad thing about my car.  All compliments.  It may have something to do with the fact I am 6'4" 225 lbs but I doubt it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gerald||10-29-2001||05:20 PM||||I took my car in to get the starter replaced. ( I would of did it myself but it was really cold) Being at my dads at the time I was in a small town and the owner of the shop called it a Forro and said that ya dont see many o them around anymore. Guess what he said next. " well we might not be able to find the part, might have to go to the next town to get it." Well they did have the part in town. No surprise there. To wich I told him that GM used that engine in like a million cars. Im guessing more now. Bloody irgnorent hicks.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000009||NorthernFiero||10-29-2001||05:44 PM|||| Yeah MinnGreenGT is right the guys and girls in the auto shop loved my se and there all into the street racing scene. But one guy could not under stand why the engine was in the trunk.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Mike||||reg||7
Z||000010||LT1 Chop Top||10-29-2001||05:54 PM||||I have certainly had mixed reactions to both of my Fieros.  Seems people either like them or love them.  I got an email for a guy that only said "Big Friggin Deal" in reference to my "Chop Top" video.  Turns out he is a Z06 guy and doesn't even have a Fiero (why hang out on a Fiero Forum then???).<BR>At shows, I would say 90% of what I hear is very positive, the other is from people that don't really seem to know what they are looking at.  It would be like me commenting on the old Fairlane I know nothing about.<BR>When it comes to shops, I am fortunate enough to have a mechanic that has a Fiero himself, and LOVES working on them.  I no longer have to deal with the shops that "won't work on Fiero's."<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/c12_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Spektrum-87GT||10-29-2001||07:47 PM||||i've also gotten mixed responses to mine. People that dont know anything about cars at all, and act like they know everything, seem to hate it and start saying they all caught on fire. The people that actually know a thing or two love it. I think anyone who makes fun of them is ignorant or just has a really small penis and is trying to make up for it with snide remarks.||||reg||1
Z||000012||neohio||10-29-2001||08:10 PM||||Heres the problem...fear of the unknown! these people have heard so many horror stories about these cars they are scared to death to work on them..I took mine(the last time I will ever take it there!)to a muffler shop and the guy put a new cat on it..anyhow he didnt weld it right so there was a leak in it so I brought it back and he had a fit! "your bitching about that little leak!" he welded it and the car didnt quite down much more so his reply was "the rods must be bad, it sounds like its gonna blow up" it had a small hole in the muffler that I fixed. I hate people that don't open there minds to new things!||||reg||6
Z||000013||DR650SE||10-29-2001||08:12 PM||||Spektrum is right.  I have a big penis and thats how I know that these cars are awesome.  Right on Spektrum.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000014||Galen||10-29-2001||08:29 PM||||I've gotten to the point where I dont care what everyone thinks about my car. As I think I have said before, its mine(sorta).. its paid for.. anyone who dislikes it, can sod off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe<P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||1
Z||000015||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||08:37 PM||||Pure Ignorance.  Same reason people hate mustangs.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||lowCG||10-29-2001||08:43 PM||||I'm a sports car junkie,and those people that snub their noses just aren't(or they wouldn't knock a mid-engined car).<BR>Sort of like cat-people,and dog-people I suppose.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||rigdonhome||10-29-2001||09:43 PM||||I've owned a lot of fast, bad-ass vehicles of all kinds over the years, and no matter what you own, there's a group of assholes somewhere that hate your vehicle.<P>I suppose it's just like society...  No matter where you're from or where you live, there is a group of people who hate you just because of petty differences.  <P>I just wish this dark trait of human nature didn't hold true for GearHeads, but unfortunately it sneaks into all aspects of humanity.<P>Ignore them...  You'll live longer without the stress.  They are less evolved and you probably wouldn't be able to get through to them if you had 100 years to try.<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000018||My7Fieros||10-29-2001||10:58 PM||||Anytime some "mechanic" calls your car "junk" and then says "I dont know, I'll give you a call in a week or so", you say, "Tell you what, dont bother, jerk", then you leave.<BR>You DONT give your business to some a$$hole w/ that kind of an atttitude.||||reg||13
Z||000019||FieroMaster88||10-29-2001||11:04 PM||||You guys have it all wrong.  They hate our cars because they are <B>Jealous</B>, not because if ignorance.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Get it right.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  Actually, I think most people are jealous.  I only spent $4000 on my car and it looks better than their $10K car!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||87FieroGTx||10-30-2001||12:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Pure Ignorance.  Same reason people hate mustangs.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Huh? How can someone be ignorant of a mustang? Other than a few parts sheet metal and badges There just like every other american made performance car!<P> Engine in front hooked to a trans hooked to a driveshaft hooked to a rear end hooked to tires. this is the same formula with most american cars.<P> Don't get me wrong BS95 I LOVE stangs, I just don't agree with anything that comes out of your mouth.<P> IMHO If you know a Camaro you know a Mustang.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||13
Z||000021||Smokin' GT||10-30-2001||12:16 AM||||You know, my neighbor is an amazing mechanic, he worked for GM for 25 years and although admitting that the first couple years the car had some problems but would tell you as one of the many opinionated mechanics of the world (shouldn't they have some "opinionated mechanics organization?") that the fiero is a very well designed car and he actually offered to buy mine!  I personally have also gotten mixed reactions, but mostly good, in fact after doing some crazy doughnuts in a parking lot the other day, someone actually got in their car and drove over just to tell me that I had an "awesome car."  I personally think the GT's (sorry guys, but just the looks) are gorgeous and performance wise, the fiero is one of THE BEST tuners you could buy.||||reg||14
Z||000022||Cheever3000||10-30-2001||12:41 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR>Anytime some "mechanic" calls your car "junk" and then says "I dont know, I'll give you a call in a week or so", you say, "Tell you what, dont bother, jerk", then you leave.<BR>You DONT give your business to some a$$hole w/ that kind of an atttitude.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><B>Exactly!</B><P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||WhiteFieroBlur||10-30-2001||02:26 AM||||I love owning this car and getting so much attention. At every single red light I am at, the car next to me always shoots off ahead of me and wants to race. These people think my fiero is some kind of race car. Sometimes I'll act like I am racing them and sometimes I won't. I could swear some old lady raced me one day in some old beat up car. Everyone always tells me they saw me here one day and there. My fiero used to break down when I first got it and everyone always knew I broke down. Thats when I had the bad reputation among people that the fieros really are crap. But since then I am all fixing it up and no break down (knock on some major wood). <P> I have recently had my first muffler shop tottaly dis me and deny me and I felt terrible. You would think everyone would love working on this thing. Now I am no mechanic but the fiero does not look like rocket science to fix. Now some of the new cars looks like you have to be a rocket sceintist to know whats goin on. <P> But I think people are jelous if your fiero is all nice lookin and everything. Like he said we can pay 1,000 or so for one and make it look sportier and nicer than any car we see driving around. I know in thier minds they wish they could have a fiero too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||fieroX||10-30-2001||02:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Anytime some "mechanic" calls your car "junk" and then says "I dont know, I'll give you a call in a week or so", you say, "Tell you what, dont bother, jerk", then you leave.<BR>You DONT give your business to some a$$hole w/ that kind of an atttitude.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>thats why I do everything myself, I cant trust anybody but myself, and my close friends, so I take things into my own hands.<P><P>------------------<BR>previously known as pontiacs4me for the first 500 posts.||||reg||1
Z||000025||artherd||10-30-2001||03:47 AM||||I got asked today "what kind of Ferrari is that?" again, and a Cobra (Shelby factory replica, real 427, show quality paint.) owner told me he really liked the car, and that it  "Looks *great* did you just repaint it?!" (He lives just up the street from me, I invited him down and showed him the Northstar engine going into the silver car, he's like "co000000ol"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>God, I love this car.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000026||FieroGTChile87||10-30-2001||03:57 AM||||I get mostly compliments on my GT but there are a few ignorant people. <P>After blowing the motor on my SE, I took it to a shop where they put in a rebuilt motor. They did nothing but complain about the car and I went through two of their rebuilt motors. Each one lasted 4,000 miles. They told me that it's because Fiero's are junk.<P>------------------<BR>Maroon 87 GT<BR>Gold 87 SE V6 (Disabled)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroGTChile_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||johnt671||10-30-2001||07:46 AM||||I get a lot of complements about the condition of my 84, usually followed by the ? don't they burn up a lot.  When I tell them that mine hasn't burnt in 206,000 miles they go into shock.  Some even go to check the odometer.||||reg||1
Z||000028||stimpy||10-30-2001||01:55 PM||||I very rarely hear anything negative about my car. I imagine one reason is that Oklahoma City is a big GM town, so there isn't any anti-American sentiment lying around here, even from the import owners. I've had people ask me what year it is and are visibly shocked when I tell them it's an 86. <P>That, and like Falconhulk says, being 6'6" and 300 lbs probably discourages smart-ass comments to some degree. ||||reg||1
Z||000029||LZeitgeist||10-30-2001||02:32 PM||||I have never, ever heard a single bad word about either of the Fieros I've owned. That's because when they get that look on their face that they're about to say something negative about my car, I nail 'em right between the eyes with a tire iron.<P>My theory that 'unconscious people can't say bad things about my car' has nearly been completely proven into fact. I only need to whac... um, I mean, discuss things with about three more people to finalize the results.<P>(O.K., maybe it's not an orthodox method, but it keeps the complaints down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000030||TylerB11||10-30-2001||02:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> It may have something to do with the fact I am 6'4" 225 lbs but I doubt it. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Damn dude, do you use a giant shoe horn to get in the car? I'm 6 feet tall and I feel tight in my fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Indiana_resto_guy||10-30-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero*101:<BR><B>Is it just me or is where ever we go there is alwas sombody that totally hates our cars?<BR>This was a wile ago but it just came to me reading these other posts. I went to get my exhaust redone at this shop and the guy was like what is it again? and I was like its a 1986 Fiero and he was like 4 banger? and i was like No its a V6 and he said i thought only the GT came w/ a v6 and i was like no go look at my car and he was like doesnt matter much to me any way and then he looked out side the window at my car and was like how do you spell FIERO? and as i started to spell it for him(not knowing that he was being an ASS HOLE!) was like JUNK thats right Plastic JUNK!<BR>well i just looked at him and said yeah what ever can you do this for me or not and he was like i dont know maybe ill have to look up and see if i can get parts any more. Ill give you a call next week. Well as the next week came no call.<BR>So i ask you fellow Fiero lovers do you get this same treatment?<BR>and why do they think our cars are Plastic Junk??<BR>Just curious to see what you guys and girls have to say   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>sorry it was so long<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have you found a shop to install a new exhaust yet?<BR>Bring it ove and I'll hang one for you.<BR>Ka-ching $$<P>||||reg||1
