Z||000036||FieroKyle||10-30-2001||10:24 PM||||Exactly, pretty much everyobne has told me Fieros are great cars for many reasons. Many kids at m,y school love my car because of what it is. Since you can put body kits and fits most GM motors in them easily, many people really like that. I also get people who think the car is pretty damn fast for a 16 year old 2.8, with a 6 in it. But since most kids at school are driving 80's car, (the fiero was a lot faster than most cars then compared to new cars of today), its viewed as one of the best cars in the school. Not to brag or get a big head, but uh thats what people tell me.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000037||FieroKyle||10-30-2001||10:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Pure Ignorance.  Same reason people hate mustangs.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya know, sometimes you really piss me off, then sometimes (its rare but sometimes) I totally agree with what you say. Then when ya said this reply, I sorta laughed to myself. Its usually the Mustang people who rant on how a piece of crap my Fiero is and how great their car is. (This especially shows in the 5.0 owners) and how their V8 is just gonna blow away my car like it was standing still. Not saying you are one (but sometimes I wonder) or some actual people who don't do that. Then I race those people and definetly change their minds. They begin to see one of two things: 1. wow that little bugger itsn't that slow for a stock V-6, or 2. imagine the potential of this car, I better watch myself when racing another one.<BR>Just my 2 and 1/2 cent raise.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">     <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000038||artherd||10-31-2001||01:07 AM||||hehhe, I belive that phrase was used as well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Yeah, it should be a real socks knocker-offer when the hood is poped.  Somehow you just KNOW that evil firebreathing cammy looking thing just dosen't belong there....  (or you are kept up late nices thinking it DOES belong there, and mentally catalouge where you can scrape and save to get it in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B> <BR>I'm guessing that what he meant was "Holy Sheeyit!"<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000039||BlackStang95||10-31-2001||02:12 AM||||Eh...we covered this before kyle.  maybe the 5.0's talk trash cuz any year stock for stock they can beat your car, some years by a lot.  You'll also be hard-pressed to convince them your fiero has more potential than their car (which they can get to 500 hp without an engine swap).||||reg||1
Z||000040||FieroKyleatSchool||10-31-2001||12:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Eh...we covered this before kyle.  maybe the 5.0's talk trash cuz any year stock for stock they can beat your car, some years by a lot.  You'll also be hard-pressed to convince them your fiero has more potential than their car (which they can get to 500 hp without an engine swap).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, I don't doubt they can do that with their engines. But not everything about a car is how good it can light them up and how fast it goes. I know pretty much all 5.0s can beat a Fiero, they should, they have a V-8. I just like how they talk trash on my car, then hide when they see a Vette rolling in or a Trans Am.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000041||Formula88||10-31-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Eh...we covered this before kyle.  maybe the 5.0's talk trash cuz any year stock for stock they can beat your car, some years by a lot.  You'll also be hard-pressed to convince them your fiero has more potential than their car (which they can get to 500 hp without an engine swap).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.freakygamers.com/smilies/s/contrib/blackeye/lol.gif"> <P>Yeah, and a 5.0 V8 owner talking trash because he can beat a 2.8 V6 owner is one of the reasons we don't respect most 5.0 ownwers.  You don't see Vette or T/A owners getting the same disrespect.  You want respect, don't talk trash.  Most people who talk trash like that - talk is all they got. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000042||ChopTop||10-31-2001||02:37 PM||||Why do they hate our cars?<P>Basically, we are still suffering from the negative publicity that was generated by the Fiero fires.  The fires were widely publicized in newspapers, television, magazines, and people were constantly reminded of it year in and year out while the car was in production and for several years after it wasn't (a melting car makes great visual footage).  That's a difficult legacy to shake, just ask a Corvair fan how bad publicity can affect peoples perceptions.  To a lesser extent it may also be due to the car's lack of performance when it was first introduced.  GM designed a car that reminded people of a Ferrari, but without the performance of one.  Akin to a mortal sin to sports car lovers.  <BR>The best way to combat the car's bad rep is by keeping it clean and in good running order, and by telling the people how good a car its been for you.<BR>BTW, bad businesses don't get my money, and I take great pleasure in letting them know that.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000043||Ferrari_cdn||10-31-2001||02:53 PM||||I have never heard anything negative about my car, except from a coworker at my pizza hut who advised me not to get a Fiero because she has heard it was a bad car when she was looking for a car (and ended up purchasing a '98 Sunfire GT for the price of a regular Sunfire).  I explained her about the car and she understood and told me to  have fun in it.  When I brought my car to work everyone was like "cool!"  Been getting some neck-turning attention when I drive around.  Just have not heard any negative comments, yet.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||7
